{"title":"a tomato heart a day","link":"https://keningzhu.com/journal/tomato-heart","date":1785399594000,"content":" \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n    \n  \n\n    \n\n    \n\n    \n      <figure>\n        \n      \n        \n          \n      \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/23a5293d-5eaf-48e4-b863-167bffbd58a3/IMG_0321.jpeg?format=1000w\" width=\"4032\" height=\"3024\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/23a5293d-5eaf-48e4-b863-167bffbd58a3/IMG_0321.jpeg?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/23a5293d-5eaf-48e4-b863-167bffbd58a3/IMG_0321.jpeg?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/23a5293d-5eaf-48e4-b863-167bffbd58a3/IMG_0321.jpeg?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/23a5293d-5eaf-48e4-b863-167bffbd58a3/IMG_0321.jpeg?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/23a5293d-5eaf-48e4-b863-167bffbd58a3/IMG_0321.jpeg?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/23a5293d-5eaf-48e4-b863-167bffbd58a3/IMG_0321.jpeg?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/23a5293d-5eaf-48e4-b863-167bffbd58a3/IMG_0321.jpeg?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n        \n      \n    \n        \n      \n\n      \n        <figcaption>\n          \n        </figcaption>\n      \n    \n      </figure>\n    \n\n    \n\n\n  \n\n  \n\n\n\n\n  <p><strong>from </strong><a href=\"https://keningonline.squarespace.com/journal/tag/marseille\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>marseille</strong></a><strong> | visit my </strong><a href=\"https://keningonline.squarespace.com/journal/tag/sketchbook\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>sketchbook</strong></a></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n  <hr />\n  \n    \n\n    \n\n\n\n  \n\n \n\n\n  <p>I learned that in french it’s called <em>coeur de boeuf </em>which<em> literally means “heart of beef.” </em>the ones that grow in south of France are almost too beautiful to eat, and when you cut them, they bleed. my friends have a garden that I water every morning, and I only pick the tomatos that are so ripe that I feel like they must leave. </p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n    \n  \n\n    \n\n    \n\n    \n      <figure>\n        \n      \n        \n          \n      \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/6a973742-97ff-4635-81f2-40cda3cccc11/IMG_0365.jpeg?format=1000w\" width=\"4032\" height=\"3024\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/6a973742-97ff-4635-81f2-40cda3cccc11/IMG_0365.jpeg?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/6a973742-97ff-4635-81f2-40cda3cccc11/IMG_0365.jpeg?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/6a973742-97ff-4635-81f2-40cda3cccc11/IMG_0365.jpeg?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/6a973742-97ff-4635-81f2-40cda3cccc11/IMG_0365.jpeg?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/6a973742-97ff-4635-81f2-40cda3cccc11/IMG_0365.jpeg?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/6a973742-97ff-4635-81f2-40cda3cccc11/IMG_0365.jpeg?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/6a973742-97ff-4635-81f2-40cda3cccc11/IMG_0365.jpeg?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n        \n      \n    \n        \n      \n\n      \n        <figcaption>\n          \n        </figcaption>\n      \n    \n      </figure>\n    \n\n    \n\n\n  \n\n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n\n  <hr />\n  \n    \n\n    \n\n\n\n  \n\n \n\n\n  <p>I ate garden tomatoes everyday, but only painted two — in both cases, I picked them first, ate the less aesthetically captivating ones, and these started to get soft, and I felt stressed that I needed to eat them. but first, I had to paint them. why??? just because I decided that I would. </p><p>my intention to paint was taking up space in my brain — the tomato sat on the garden table for days, like unfinished business. these weeks, I’ve had more visuals in my head than I have time to paint them. but, still lives are more straightforward than the imaginal sensations in my head. they are here. they are waiting for me. </p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n    \n  \n\n    \n\n    \n\n    \n      <figure>\n        \n      \n        \n          \n      \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/0b4a8821-d3a2-4b47-a85c-fc0631bddb43/IMG_0320.jpeg?format=1000w\" width=\"4032\" height=\"3024\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/0b4a8821-d3a2-4b47-a85c-fc0631bddb43/IMG_0320.jpeg?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/0b4a8821-d3a2-4b47-a85c-fc0631bddb43/IMG_0320.jpeg?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/0b4a8821-d3a2-4b47-a85c-fc0631bddb43/IMG_0320.jpeg?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/0b4a8821-d3a2-4b47-a85c-fc0631bddb43/IMG_0320.jpeg?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/0b4a8821-d3a2-4b47-a85c-fc0631bddb43/IMG_0320.jpeg?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/0b4a8821-d3a2-4b47-a85c-fc0631bddb43/IMG_0320.jpeg?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/0b4a8821-d3a2-4b47-a85c-fc0631bddb43/IMG_0320.jpeg?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n        \n      \n    \n        \n      \n\n      \n        <figcaption>\n          \n        </figcaption>\n      \n    \n      </figure>\n    \n\n    \n\n\n  \n\n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n\n  <hr />\n  \n    \n\n    \n\n\n\n  \n\n \n\n\n  <p>at first, I didn’t understand why I started to cry when drawing/painting this first tomato. by the time I painted the second one, I did. because. <em>coeur de boeuf. </em>it is too much like a heart — bovine, alien, or human. its skin is so thin, it is so easily bruised (I even dropped them), it is both ambiguously vegetal and fruity. it smells like something green and fresh, but it tastes like flesh of the earth. it is oddly shaped and bulbous; it is offering itself to you, and ready to be sliced open and eaten, ready to bleed onto the plate, in your mouth. it is the heart offering of summer. </p><p>this is why I painted the second tomato heart with a knife. </p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n    \n  \n\n    \n\n    \n\n    \n      <figure>\n        \n      \n        \n          \n      \n        \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          \n          <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/caed0d79-916a-400f-ba01-bd7a60a4bf2a/IMG_0413.jpg?format=1000w\" width=\"4032\" height=\"3024\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/caed0d79-916a-400f-ba01-bd7a60a4bf2a/IMG_0413.jpg?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/caed0d79-916a-400f-ba01-bd7a60a4bf2a/IMG_0413.jpg?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/caed0d79-916a-400f-ba01-bd7a60a4bf2a/IMG_0413.jpg?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/caed0d79-916a-400f-ba01-bd7a60a4bf2a/IMG_0413.jpg?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/caed0d79-916a-400f-ba01-bd7a60a4bf2a/IMG_0413.jpg?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/caed0d79-916a-400f-ba01-bd7a60a4bf2a/IMG_0413.jpg?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/caed0d79-916a-400f-ba01-bd7a60a4bf2a/IMG_0413.jpg?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n        \n      \n    \n        \n      \n\n      \n        <figcaption>\n          \n        </figcaption>\n      \n    \n      </figure>\n    \n\n    \n\n\n  \n\n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n\n  <hr />\n  \n    \n\n    \n\n\n\n  \n\n \n\n\n  <p>do I, perhaps, overly identify with / anthropomorphize my tomatoes? definitely. does it make my life easier? probably not. is a tomato just a damn tomato? yeah. is <strong><em>how I feel</em></strong> so inextricably intertwined with <strong><em>what I see</em></strong>? yes. this continues to be true, as <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/journal/arriving-seeing-perceiving\" target=\"_blank\">I wrote about last week</a>. <br /><br />I’ve always found that painting fruit still lives is always satisfyingly meditative and slow. a part of my brain is nagging and saying <em>“you don’t have time for this!”</em> and I tell it to calm down. I set a timer for 23 minutes (it takes me 2-3 of those), put on some music, and start recreating my vegetable heart, on the page. </p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n    \n  \n\n    \n\n    \n\n    \n      <figure>\n        \n      \n        \n          \n      \n        